Package: gnome-shell-extension-multizoom
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Woody1193 <Woody1193@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 42~), gnome-shell (<< 43~), gir1.2-atspi-2.0, gir1.2-adw-1
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-prefs
Homepage: https://github.com/Woody1193/multizoom
Description: GNOME Shell screen zoom that treats each monitor separately
 MultiZoom magnifies each monitor on its own. Only the monitor with the
 pointer or keyboard focus follows it; the others keep their view, and any
 monitor's view can be locked in place.
